<article class="env-lemma" id="0H98">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H98">Lemma <span data-tag="0H98">18.24.1</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C},\mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finitely presented $\mathcal{O}$-module. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{G} \to \mathcal{F}$ be a morphism of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. If $\mathcal{G}$ is finite type, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(\varphi )$ is finitely presented. </p>
